SOPA WORKING STEPS
SOPA is a true mess..follow these steps

SOPA RUN WITH CLI SUCCESSFULLY

0. Work always in the same directory folder during all the steps
1.Download the xenium dataset from 10x webpage or the links saved in STAT3D page
2.Extract the files and create a new folder called "sopa_directory" which must contain these files : experiment.xenium, morphology_mip and _focus, transcripts. parquest. Since it is not really clear which other files to include, I include them all except for morphology.ome.tiff
3.Install sopa with downgraded cellpose to v3.0.8 (it should be v3, not v4) use conda and install sopa : pip install sopa[cellpose], pip uninstall cellpose, pip install cellpose==3.0.8
4.convert the sopa_directory in .zarr (SpatialData sdata) format : sopa convert sopa_directory --technology xenium 
5.run : set SOPA_PARALLELIZATION_BACKEND=dask
6.sopa patchify image sopa_directory.zarr --patch-width-pixel 1900 --patch-overlap-pixel 150 # make patches for low-memory segmentation, you must use 1900 OR 2000 not higher than that because otherwise the distribution of the data on 4 workers will be killed,
the workers will not have enough memory space for allocating the data, 1900 creates 224 patches (before I created 14 patches, while the automatic patching created 24 , too few, the data processign was too heavy).You can use 2000 and 150 or 1900 and 150.Sopa suggests 6000 , which is wrong !
7.run : sopa segmentation cellpose sopa_directory.zarr --diameter 30 --channels DAPI --gpu
8. do not use the environment sopa with snakefile, it is not needed and gives strange errors
9.Do not need to resolve the segmentation with : sopa resolve cellpose sopa_directory.zarr # resolve segmentation conflicts at boundaries, it is done automatically
10.run : sopa aggregate sopa_directory.zarr --aggregate-channels --min-transcripts 10 (use the config file to check the parameters, this does not work :sopa aggregate sopa_directory.zarr --average-intensities, but they still suggest it even if is wrong)
11.run time with supercomputer HCP dataset in gpu : 48 minutes, 6 hours with my laptop (SOPA did not test the datasets they talk about (except for merscope, maybe) for the time efficiency they created a test dataset explained in supplementary data)
11.1 Annotation sopa annotate tangram "sopa annotate tangram sopa_directory.zarr --sc-reference-path adata_reference.h5ad --cell-type-key cell_type" #"Tangram is a transcript-based annotation that uses an annotated single-cell reference.
Let's suppose your reference AnnData object is stored in a file called adata_reference.h5ad (preferably, keep raw counts), and the cell type is in adata.obs["cell_type"]. Then, you can annotate your spatial data with the command above.
11.2 in conda install tangram : pip install tangram-sc
11.3 Create your AnnData file with references like this : In R create a data frame for the ref Human Primary.. from celldex , since online they are difficult to find. The generation of the hd5a is performed through one R script and 
one python script subsequentially, which are saved in /test_sopa. First the R script extracts the ref info and saved three csv files with the info ( label.main name is changed into cell_type, since sopa reads only this name). Python scripts accesses the excel files
and creates the anndata file. The anndata needs to be saved in the same folder where also sopa_direcotry.zarr is saved.
12.Get the report: sopa report sopa_HCP_directory.zarr report.html





sopa explorer write sopa_directory.zarr # convert for interactive vizualisation



